# Escape never changes the window's size (CraCore WindowEscape, 11 Nov 2026). AppKit's own
# cancelOperation: took a full-screen window out of full screen; CraWindow now hands Escape to its
# controller, which only closes what is open (or a page's video full screen). A maximized window
# stays maximized; with the command bar open, Escape closes the bar and the window stays as it was.
cra://debug?windowSize=1000x700
wait 2
cra://debug?zoomWindow=1
wait 1.5
cra://debug?windowState=zoomed
expect-log window state zoomed: main0 .*docked=1
cra://debug?windowEscape=1
wait 1
expect-log escape in window: nothing
cra://debug?windowState=afterEscape
reject-log window state afterEscape: main0 .*size=1000x700
cra://action/newTab
wait 1
cra://debug?windowEscape=1
wait 1
expect-log escape in window: dismissOpen
cra://debug?commandBarState=closed
expect-log command bar closed: open=0
